troller I usually read an entity from the database with all the associations needed for the view then use patchEntity to update the entity with form data.\r\n\r\nThis is how I do it:\r\n\r\n- Read entity and associations for the view.\r\n- Is POST:\r\n  - Patch entity.\r\n  - Save.\r\n  - If OK then redirect.\r\n- Read additional data for dropdowns, etc.\r\n\r\nI could do this instead:\r\n\r\n- Read entity.\r\n- Is POST:\r\n  - Patch entity.\r\n  - Save.\r\n  - If OK then redirect.\r\n- Read associations (loadInto).\r\n- Read additional data for dropdowns, etc.\r\n\r\nBut when saving fails, the data of the associated enties edited by the user would be lost when reading associations. Think of an article form that lets you edit the status of comments.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/comments/406254174/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"berarma","id":162766,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2Mjc2Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/162766?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma","html_url":"https://github.com/berarma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/berarma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.c